# Spectral types: Yale Bright Star Catalog, 5th ed. (fallback: Hipparcos via HYG).
# Magnitudes: HYG v4.1 (Hipparcos-derived Johnson V); combined light for unresolved
#   multiples. Many bright stars are variable, so treat the ranking as approximate.
# Formal names: Bayer designation, else Flamsteed, else HR (Bright Star) number.
# Common names: IAU-approved proper names as listed in HYG v4.1.
# Only stars with a Hipparcos entry are included, so each resolved component
#   (e.g. Alpha1/Alpha2 Centauri) appears once; the cutoff falls within a tie at V = 3.54.
#
